  "tagline": "Open-source native XML database and XQuery application platform for documents and digital editions.",
  "description": "eXist-db is a Java native XML database that stores documents in a collection hierarchy and queries them with XQuery 3.1, XPath and XSLT. Lucene powers its full-text indexes, and range indexes cover structured queries. It doubles as an application server: XQuery modules, RESTXQ endpoints and packaged apps run inside the database, which is why it is a mainstay of digital humanities, TEI editions and publishing workflows. The 6.x line is stable (6.4.1, March 2026), and 7.0 is in beta. It is not built for large-scale transactional work, but it is excellent for XML-heavy content applications.",
